-- Describe external_listings: all 25 columns (2 of 25 had a COMMENT ON COLUMN before, organization_id and sold_at; catalog
-- count on prod, 2026-10-07) and a corrected table comment. Comments only.
-- Describe stage of the repair loop (docs/ledger/theory/data-machine-cases.md section 12; data-machine.md
-- "the database describes itself"). Written table in the atlas (2 updates since the statistics counters began): 139,760
-- rows on 2026-10-07 12:50Z by exact count (the atlas estimate of 139,309 is a stale pg_class.reltuples); the newest row
-- was created 2026-04-14 02:36Z and the newest write is an update at 2026-10-06 00:49Z.
--
-- METHOD (read 2026-10-07 12:49-13:05Z UTC):
--   Columns, types, defaults, constraints, indexes, triggers, policies, grants (has_table_privilege and
--   has_any_column_privilege for anon and authenticated) and existing comments from pg_attribute, pg_attrdef,
--   pg_constraint, pg_indexes, pg_trigger, pg_policy and pg_description; the foreign keys that point at the table from
--   pg_constraint; the one view that reads it from pg_depend. Fill, platform and status counts, listing_id and URL shapes
--   (host and first path segment, ids masked), date windows, price and count distributions, the match of platform against
--   observation_sources.slug, the orphan vehicle ids (anti-join against vehicles) and listing_url_key against
--   normalize_listing_url_key(listing_url) are exact counts over the whole table (73 MB heap, 720 MB TOAST, read only).
--   The metadata keys, the lot-number comparison, the reserve status of sold rows, the vehicle_events successor rows (same
--   source_url) and the vehicles that enrich_cross_ref_ext_price would write come from a 5% block sample (TABLESAMPLE
--   SYSTEM (5) REPEATABLE (20261007), 6,791 rows, the sample of docs/proposals/2026-10-07-platform-entity.md), because
--   metadata is 720 MB of TOAST and the exact join for the last count exceeded the 10 s timeout. "Filled" means non-NULL.
--   Writers and readers from code at origin/main d93ddafd8 (supabase/functions, supabase/migrations, scripts,
--   nuke_frontend/src, mcp-server, apps; also the tree before commit 216f9c545 for the former writers): the creating
--   migration 20251103000002_notification_system.sql; 20260112000002_external_listings_url_key_dedupe.sql;
--   20260927170100_testimony_fks_restrict_not_cascade.sql; the bodies, read with pg_get_functiondef, of the 32 live
--   functions in any non-system schema whose body names the table and of the five trigger functions on it; the trigger
--   sync_bid_count_trigger on vehicles; cron.job (one job, reconcile-listing-status, jobid 184, inactive); pg_depend (the
--   view sold_vehicle_proof); write_receipts (no rows: the table carries no receipt trigger); pg_stat_user_tables;
--   pipeline_registry (1 table-level row, owned_by retired, from 20261007002507_declare_table_owners_1.sql; no row is
--   added or changed here). Reader code: nuke_frontend/src/pages/vehicle-profile/loadVehicleData.ts
--   (get_vehicle_profile_data), DiscoveryFeed.tsx and PriceAnalysisPanel.tsx (vehicle_price_signal),
--   SoldInventoryBrowser.tsx (sold_vehicle_proof), supabase/functions/extract-bat-core (compute_vehicle_grade) and
--   score-live-auctions (score_closed_predictions); scripts/market/replay-live-lot-reader.sql and three monitoring SQL
--   files read it by hand.
-- LIMITS:
--   Rows are overwritten in place, so the table keeps the last write only. The metadata facts, the successor share and the
--   enrich_cross_ref_ext_price count come from a 5% block sample and can miss rare cases. How the 14,422 orphan rows lost
--   their vehicle is not recorded. Currency is not stored on the row. pg_stat_user_tables counters began at an unrecorded
--   time (the server last started 2026-09-29 09:20Z). The table holds public auction-site handles (seller_username and
--   buyer_username in metadata) and listing URLs: quoted values are platform and status codes, URL shapes with ids masked,
--   key names, column and function names, aggregate prices and counts only; no handle, URL, vehicle id or price of one
--   listing.
-- CHANGED EXISTING COMMENTS:
--   Table: it said "RETIRED in favor of vehicle_events (commit 216f9c545 moved its writers there; no rows since
--   2026-04-14). Legacy listing table (BaT, Cars and Bids, eBay Motors and others): one row per vehicle listing on a
--   platform (grain: vehicle x platform listing). Superseded for new listings by vehicle_events (commit 216f9c545). No edge
--   function writes it in the repo; SQL maintenance functions still name it (reconcile_listing_status,
--   cleanup_stale_listings, merge_duplicate_listings). Rows created 2025-12-07 .. 2026-04-14, none since; 1 row write
--   since the statistics reset." The retirement stays as the opening; the new comment adds the writer that still updates
--   rows (the bid-count trigger on vehicles, 2 updates now), the readers, the anon read paths and the anon-callable writer
--   of vehicles.sale_price, the orphans, the platform spellings and the clocks.
--   Column organization_id: it said "Organization that owns/manages this listing. NULL for imported external listings
--   (BaT, etc.) that are not associated with a specific organization." On 1,671 of the 1,751 filled rows the value is the
--   auction house itself, not a seller; the new comment keeps the intent and says what the values are.
--   Column sold_at: its text opens the new comment unchanged; fill, writers, readers, unit, source, grain and clock are
--   added.

BEGIN;
SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '30s';
SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s';

COMMENT ON TABLE public.external_listings IS
'RETIRED in favor of vehicle_events (commit 216f9c545, 2026-03-07, moved its writers there; no row created since 2026-04-14). Legacy listing table: one row per listing of a vehicle on an auction or sale platform (grain: one platform listing; listing_url and listing_url_key are distinct on every row). 139,760 rows on 2026-10-07 for 137,844 vehicle ids. By platform: bat 103,978, barrettjackson 25,752, pcarmarket 6,224, bonhams 2,066, cars_and_bids 1,275, mecum 273, collecting_cars 70, sbx 38, broad_arrow 31, rmsothebys 22, classic_com 11, gooding 9, hagerty 7, blocket 3, craigslist 1. By listing_status: sold 109,831, ended 25,716, active 4,038 (stale), unsold 142, pending 28, cancelled 5. Created 2025-12-07 .. 2026-04-14 (by month: 2025-12 1,620, 2026-01 34,989, 2026-02 96,289, 2026-03 6,625, 2026-04 237) by the extractors (extract-bat-core, extract-barrett-jackson, extract-bonhams, import-pcarmarket-listing, extract-cars-and-bids-core, extract-mecum, extract-broad-arrow, extract-gooding and others); after commit 216f9c545 the deployed copies still inserted bat rows until 2026-03-07 23:04Z, bonhams until 2026-03-15 and pcarmarket until 2026-04-14. In a 5% block sample 6,724 of 6,791 rows (99.0%) have a vehicle_events row with the same source_url. Writers today (pipeline_registry owner retired, do_not_write_directly true): the trigger sync_bid_count_trigger on vehicles (AFTER UPDATE OF bid_count) runs sync_bid_count_to_external_listings, which raises bid_count and stamps updated_at on the listings of the vehicle whose count is lower; it made the 3 updates after 2026-04-14 (2026-09-27 twice and 2026-10-06 00:49Z; each row now carries the vehicle bid_count). merge_vehicle_into_primary_by_url moves vehicle_id to the surviving vehicle or deletes the row when the survivor already holds the same platform and listing_id, without touching updated_at. Maintenance functions that write it have no caller in cron.job or the repo: reconcile_listing_status (its cron job reconcile-listing-status, jobid 184, is inactive), cleanup_stale_listings, fix_external_listings_missing_prices, merge_duplicate_listings and backfill_missing_bat_external_listings. pg_stat_user_tables since its counters began (the server last started 2026-09-29 09:20Z): 0 inserts, 2 updates and 0 deletes; 18 sequential scans; index scans 1,197,694 at 12:49Z and 1,200,743 at 12:58Z, reads that keep arriving (the bid-count trigger probes the table by vehicle_id on every vehicles bid_count change). Five triggers fire on writes here: trg_external_listings_url_key (BEFORE; sets listing_url_key), track_auction_transitions (timeline events through create_auction_timeline_event when the status changes), trg_sync_external_listing_to_org_vehicles (organization_vehicles links), trigger_auto_mark_vehicle_sold (vehicles sale fields and an organization_vehicles sold_by row when sold) and trigger_sync_active_auction_prices (vehicles high_bid and bid_count while active). Readers: get_vehicle_profile_data(uuid) (called by the vehicle profile page, nuke_frontend/src/pages/vehicle-profile/loadVehicleData.ts, which ignores this part of the result), vehicle_price_signal(uuid[]) (DiscoveryFeed, PriceAnalysisPanel; active rows), compute_vehicle_grade (extract-bat-core, persist_vehicle_grade), score_closed_predictions (score-live-auctions), get_vehicle_current_price (on_user_follows_vehicle), apply_approved_verification (trigger on vehicle_relationship_verifications), the view sold_vehicle_proof (SoldInventoryBrowser.tsx), and about 20 other function bodies with no caller in cron.job or the repo. The frontend now reads vehicle_events into an external_listings-shaped object and does not query this table (OrganizationProfile.tsx records the switch). Foreign keys in: auction_listing_images.external_listing_id (ON DELETE SET NULL, 367 rows) and external_auction_bids.external_listing_id (ON DELETE CASCADE, 1 of 26,164 rows). Defects (2026-10-07): 14,422 rows (10.3%) point at a vehicle id that is not in vehicles (see vehicle_id); platform matches observation_sources.slug on 81.5% of rows (see platform); 1,920 pcarmarket, 10 bat and 8 cars_and_bids sold rows carry the write clock as sold_at (see sold_at); 1,671 rows name the auction house as organization_id, and the triggers recorded it as the seller (see organization_id). Access: RLS is on with no policy, and anon and authenticated hold no privilege on the table or any column (2026-10-07). Seven SECURITY DEFINER functions open to anon (EXECUTE granted to PUBLIC, anon and authenticated) go around that: get_vehicle_profile_data returns every column of every row of any public vehicle, metadata with the seller and buyer handles included; vehicle_price_signal returns listing_url and current_bid of active rows; get_listings_needing_sync returns id, platform and listing_url of active rows; calculate_platform_revenue, check_auction_sync_health and check_sync_coverage return aggregates; and enrich_cross_ref_ext_price(integer), which has no fixed search_path, UPDATEs vehicles.sale_price from final_price for vehicles whose sale_price is NULL (116 of 6,791 rows of a 5% block sample qualify, 1.7%), so anyone with the public API key can trigger that write. The view sold_vehicle_proof (owner postgres, not security_invoker, SELECT granted to anon and authenticated) shows listing_url, platform, status, final_price, sold_at and end_date of 460 rows. No write receipts. Clocks: start_date, end_date and sold_at are event times on the platform as the extractor parsed them; created_at, updated_at and last_synced_at are database or writer times; nothing records when a value was read from the site.';

-- ── Identity and keys ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.id IS
'Surrogate key of the listing row, uuid, gen_random_uuid() default, the PRIMARY KEY. 139,760 values (2026-10-07). Referenced by auction_listing_images.external_listing_id (foreign key ON DELETE SET NULL; 367 rows) and external_auction_bids.external_listing_id (ON DELETE CASCADE; 1 of 26,164 rows). track_auction_phase_transitions passes it to create_auction_timeline_event as the source of the timeline event it writes. Unit: none (uuid). Source: column default. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.vehicle_id IS
'Vehicle the listing is for: a vehicles.id, NOT NULL, foreign key to vehicles(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT NOT VALID (ON DELETE CASCADE from the creating migration 20251103000002 until 20260927170100 switched it; enforced on new and updated rows, old rows unchecked). 137,844 distinct values on 139,760 rows (2026-10-07). 1,709 vehicles hold 2 or more rows (3,625 rows; for 1,366 of them all rows are on one platform), and one vehicle holds 107 rows, 106 of them different pcarmarket listings, so a vehicle can carry listings of other cars. 14,422 rows (10.3%) point at an id that is not in vehicles: bat 8,963, barrettjackson 5,234, mecum 83, pcarmarket 83, bonhams 39 and 20 on other platforms, created 2025-12-07 .. 2026-03-07 and last written by 2026-03-13. The key cascaded before 20260927170100, so deleting the vehicle should have removed the row; how these rows lost their vehicle (a delete or load with the RI triggers off, or rows older than the key) is not recorded, and 20260927170100 records the same pattern in vehicle_events. Part of the UNIQUE index external_listings_unique_vehicle_platform_listing (vehicle_id, platform, listing_id; a NULL listing_id never collides) and of three secondary indexes. merge_vehicle_into_primary_by_url moves it to the surviving vehicle. Unit: none (uuid). Source: the extractor that resolved the vehicle (the shared resolveVehicleForListing before commit 216f9c545). Grain: one platform listing. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.organization_id IS
'Organization recorded with the listing: an organizations.id, nullable, foreign key ON DELETE CASCADE (validated). The creating migration meant the organization that owns or manages the listing (then NOT NULL, referencing businesses); the former comment said NULL for imported external listings not associated with a specific organization. Filled on 1,751 rows (1.3%, 2026-10-07). On 1,671 of them (95.4%) it is the auction house itself, one organization per platform whose name is the house: cars_and_bids 1,195 rows, mecum 273, collecting_cars 70, sbx 38 (business_type dealer), pcarmarket 33, broad_arrow 31, rmsothebys 22, gooding 9 (the others auction_house); only 80 bat rows name 6 other organizations (70 dealer, 10 other), which are sellers. The triggers read this column as the seller: trg_sync_external_listing_to_org_vehicles and trigger_auto_mark_vehicle_sold write an organization_vehicles sold_by row for it, and 963 sold_by rows pair these vehicles with their house (cars_and_bids 951, mecum 5, pcarmarket 5, collecting_cars 2), so the house is recorded as the seller. The platform itself is linked separately through observation_sources.business_id (see platform). Read by sold_vehicle_proof (joined on vehicle and organization). Unit: none (uuid). Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.platform IS
'Platform the listing is on, a lower-case code, text NOT NULL; CHECK external_listings_platform_check in 23 codes (bat, cars_and_bids, mecum, barrettjackson, russoandsteele, pcarmarket, sbx, bonhams, rmsothebys, collecting_cars, broad_arrow, gooding, ebay_motors, facebook_marketplace, autotrader, hemmings, classic_com, craigslist, copart, iaai, hagerty, blocket, ksl), NOT VALID, which every row satisfies. 15 codes occur (2026-10-07): bat 103,978, barrettjackson 25,752, pcarmarket 6,224, bonhams 2,066, cars_and_bids 1,275, mecum 273, collecting_cars 70, sbx 38, broad_arrow 31, rmsothebys 22, classic_com 11, gooding 9, hagerty 7, blocket 3, craigslist 1. Not keyed to the platform entity. Measured against observation_sources.slug, which docs/proposals/2026-10-07-platform-entity.md proposes to declare as the platform entity and to key this column to (NOT VALID, after rows for the spellings writers emit), the code matches a slug on 113,857 of 139,760 rows (81.5%, exact, 2026-10-07; the memo 5% sample found 82%). The unmatched spellings, with the slug of their sibling: barrettjackson 25,752 (barrett-jackson; the spelling the memo names for this column), collecting_cars 70 (collecting-cars), sbx 38 (sbx-cars), rmsothebys 22 (rm-sothebys), classic_com 11 (classic-com), hagerty 7 (hagerty-marketplace) and blocket 3 (no slug). trg_sync_external_listing_to_org_vehicles (sync_external_listing_to_organization_vehicles) looks the platform organization up by that slug (lower case, spaces to dashes, plus two special cases for bringatrailer and cars and bids), so these 25,903 rows link no platform organization. The code and the URL disagree on 2 rows: 1 barrettjackson row holds a mecum.com URL and 1 a bringatrailer.com URL. Indexed as lower(platform) with vehicle_id and part of two unique indexes. Unit: none (text code). Source: the extractor constant. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.listing_url IS
'Listing page on the platform, text NOT NULL, distinct on every row (139,760 values, 2026-10-07). Hosts and first path segment: bringatrailer.com/listing/ 103,979 (every bat row and 1 barrettjackson row), barrett-jackson.com with or without www 25,750, pcarmarket.com/auction/ 6,224 (7 on numbered pcarmarket subdomains, 2 on a staging subdomain), bonhams.com or cars.bonhams.com /auction/ 2,066, carsandbids.com/auctions/ 1,275, mecum.com/lots/ 274, collectingcars.com 70, sbxcars.com 38, broadarrowauctions.com 31, rmsothebys.com 22, classic.com 11, goodingco.com 9, hagerty.com/marketplace/ 7, blocket.se 3, craigslist.org 1. The trigger trg_external_listings_url_key derives listing_url_key from it on insert and on update of this column. Public listing pages; none is quoted here. Unit: none (URL). Source: the extractor (extract-bat-core wrote its canonical URL). Grain: one platform listing. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.listing_url_key IS
'Normalised listing_url used as the dedupe key: lower case, query and fragment removed, scheme, leading www. and trailing slashes stripped (normalize_listing_url_key, 20260112000002). Set by the BEFORE trigger trg_external_listings_url_key on insert and on update of listing_url, so writers cannot set it otherwise; equal to normalize_listing_url_key(listing_url) on all 139,760 rows and distinct on every row (2026-10-07). UNIQUE with platform where not NULL (uq_external_listings_platform_url_key), the index extract-bat-core used for its manual upsert. api-v1-vehicle-auction/forecast.ts reimplements the same normalisation. Unit: none (text). Source: set_external_listings_url_key. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.listing_id IS
'Listing number on the platform, text, nullable; part of the UNIQUE index (vehicle_id, platform, listing_id), where NULLs never collide. Filled on 113,621 rows (81.3%, 2026-10-07). bat: the lot number (1 to 6 digits) on 102,986 rows, equal to metadata.lot_number on 5,011 of 5,059 rows of a 5% block sample; the full listing URL on 954 rows and a URL slug on 29, because extract-bat-core wrote the lot number or else the canonical URL; NULL on 9. bonhams: the lot number on all 2,066; mecum: the lot code (2 to 4 characters, or 7 digits) on all 273; cars_and_bids: an 8-character auction code on 1,100 of 1,275; pcarmarket: digits on 3,680 and other codes on 2,511 of 6,224; classic_com 11, hagerty 7, blocket 3 and craigslist 1 filled. NULL on every barrettjackson, collecting_cars, sbx, broad_arrow, rmsothebys and gooding row, so for those the unique index does not stop a second row; listing_url_key does. Unit: none (text). Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: n/a.';

-- ── Status and dates ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.listing_status IS
'State of the listing when it was last written, text NOT NULL, CHECK in (pending, active, ended, sold, unsold, cancelled, reserve_not_met, no_sale). 6 occur (2026-10-07): sold 109,831 (78.6%), ended 25,716, active 4,038, unsold 142, pending 28, cancelled 5; reserve_not_met and no_sale never. For bat, extract-bat-core wrote sold when it parsed a sale price above 0, else active when the end was in the future, else ended; in a 5% block sample 99 of 3,894 sold bat rows say reserve_not_met in metadata.reserve_status. Not maintained since the writers moved: the 4,038 active rows are stale (end_date past on 1,515, NULL on 2,519, future on 4), no job syncs them (last_synced_at ends 2026-01-23), and 657 active pcarmarket rows already carry a final_price. Triggers read it: trigger_auto_mark_vehicle_sold (when sold), trigger_sync_active_auction_prices (when active) and track_auction_transitions (on a change). Indexed where sold (idx_external_listings_sold_vehicle_at). Unit: none (text code). Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: as of updated_at.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.start_date IS
'When the listing opened on the platform, timestamptz, nullable. Filled on 13 rows (0.01%, 2026-10-07): 12 bat rows (2022-08 .. 2025-12) and 1 craigslist row; the extractors that wrote the other rows did not send it. Copied into the auction_started timeline event by track_auction_phase_transitions. Unit: timestamptz. Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: event time on the platform as the extractor parsed it.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.end_date IS
'When the listing closed, or was scheduled to close, on the platform, timestamptz, nullable. Filled on 107,714 rows (77.1%, 2026-10-07): bat 102,686 (2014-07-30 .. 2026-03-06; 107 at midnight UTC, where extract-bat-core had only a date), bonhams 2,066 (all at midnight UTC, 2003-02-24 .. 2026-06-13), pcarmarket 2,823, cars_and_bids 81, sbx 34, collecting_cars 17, hagerty 7; NULL on every barrettjackson, mecum, broad_arrow, rmsothebys and gooding row. Parse failures: 9 pcarmarket values before 1990 (the earliest in 1659) and 8 after 2026 (the latest in 2437), and 1 collecting_cars and 3 sbx values after 2026. Indexed with vehicle_id (idx_external_listings_vehicle_end_date). auto_mark_vehicle_sold_from_external_listing copies it to vehicles.auction_end_date and uses it as the sale day when sold_at is NULL. Unit: timestamptz. Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: event time on the platform (close) as the extractor parsed it.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.sold_at IS
'Sale instant as the listing''s lander stored it (event clock, UTC). A value with sub-second precision within 1 s of this row''s created_at or updated_at is the lander''s write clock (import-pcarmarket-listing, Feb 2026: 1,920 PCARMARKET, 10 BaT and 8 Cars & Bids sold rows on 2026-10-06), not a sale instant; auto_mark_vehicle_sold_from_external_listing does not copy it to vehicles.sale_date (trg_enforce_vehicle_sale_date_retraction, migration 20261006234500). Filled on 81,984 rows (58.7%, 2026-10-07): 81,049 sold rows and 935 rows not sold (pcarmarket 670, mecum 263, cars_and_bids 2). NULL on 28,782 sold rows, among them every barrettjackson row (25,562) and 2,548 bat rows. extract-bat-core wrote the auction end as the sale instant (equal to end_date). Ranges: bat 2014-07-30 .. 2026-02-26, bonhams 2003-02-24 .. 2026-01-30 (midnight UTC), mecum 2013-04-25 .. 2026-03-21 (23:59:59.999), pcarmarket 2026-02-10 .. 2026-04-14 (2,281 of its 2,593 values are write clocks, counting rows not sold). Indexed with vehicle_id where sold. Read by sold_vehicle_proof and the readers named in the table comment. Unit: timestamptz. Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: event time of the sale, except the write-clock rows above.';

-- ── Prices and counts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.current_bid IS
'Highest bid when the row was last written; for sold bat rows extract-bat-core wrote the sale price here. numeric, nullable. Filled on 107,628 rows (77.0%, 2026-10-07): bat 102,666, pcarmarket 3,719, cars_and_bids 1,132, collecting_cars 70, sbx 21, broad_arrow 14, hagerty 6; none on barrettjackson, bonhams, mecum, rmsothebys or gooding rows. Equal to final_price on 78,741 bat, 1,916 pcarmarket and 591 cars_and_bids rows. Whole numbers but one; 1 collecting_cars value is 0. trigger_sync_active_auction_prices copies it to vehicles.high_bid while the row is active; vehicle_price_signal reads it from active rows. Unit: the platform sale currency, not stored on the row (US dollars on the US platforms). Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: as of updated_at.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.reserve_price IS
'Reserve price of the listing, numeric, nullable. Filled on 21 rows (0.02%, 2026-10-07): cars_and_bids 20 and bat 1; auction sites rarely publish it, and metadata.reserve_status carries the reserve state instead. Read by track_auction_phase_transitions for the reserve-met event. Unit: the platform sale currency, not stored on the row. Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: as of updated_at.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.buy_now_price IS
'Fixed asking price where the platform offers one, numeric, nullable. Filled on 1 row (craigslist, 2026-10-07). Unit: the platform sale currency, not stored on the row. Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: as of updated_at.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.final_price IS
'Hammer or sale price, numeric, nullable. Filled on 110,461 rows (79.0%, 2026-10-07): 109,590 sold rows and 871 others (pcarmarket 669, bat 176, 26 on other platforms); NULL on 241 sold rows. By platform: bat 80,785 (median 22,500), barrettjackson 25,431 (median 44,000), pcarmarket 2,585, bonhams 1,042, cars_and_bids 610, mecum 5, blocket 3. All whole numbers but one, none 0 or below. The currency is not stored: the US platforms sell in US dollars, the 3 blocket values are Swedish kronor by magnitude, and the 1,042 bonhams prices carry no currency (the bonhams rows that record one in metadata.estimate_currency say GBP 260, EUR 126, CHF 22, USD 1, none of them priced). auto_mark_vehicle_sold_from_external_listing copies it (or current_bid) to vehicles.sale_price, winning_bid and high_bid when sold; enrich_cross_ref_ext_price copies it to vehicles.sale_price where that is NULL, without currency. Unit: the platform sale currency, not stored on the row. Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: as of updated_at.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.bid_count IS
'Number of bids the platform showed, integer, nullable, default 0. Above 0 on 109,084 rows, 0 on 29,007, NULL on 1,669 (pcarmarket 1,404, mecum 202, cars_and_bids 52, 11 on smaller platforms; 2026-10-07). Medians where above 0: bat 25, cars_and_bids 30, pcarmarket 16. Implausible values: 38 pcarmarket rows above 1,000 (12 above 5,000, the largest 559,850). sync_bid_count_to_external_listings (trigger on vehicles) raises it to vehicles.bid_count when that is larger, the only live writer: 7 barrettjackson rows got a count that way. Unit: bids. Source: the extractor, or the vehicles trigger. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: as of updated_at.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.view_count IS
'Page views the platform showed, integer, nullable, default 0. Above 0 on 105,767 rows (bat 100,680, pcarmarket 4,103, cars_and_bids 977, hagerty 7), NULL on 2,346 (2026-10-07); 0 elsewhere because those platforms do not show views. Median where above 0: bat 11,501. Copied to vehicles.bat_views for sold bat rows by auto_mark_vehicle_sold_from_external_listing. Unit: views. Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: as of updated_at.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.watcher_count IS
'Watchers the platform showed, integer, nullable, default 0. Above 0 on 100,785 rows (bat 100,679, cars_and_bids 106), NULL on 226 (2026-10-07). Median where above 0: bat 656. Copied to vehicles.bat_watchers for sold bat rows by auto_mark_vehicle_sold_from_external_listing. Unit: watchers. Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: as of updated_at.';

-- ── Commercial and sync fields (mostly unused) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.commission_rate IS
'Intended commission of this platform (creating migration 20251103000002: commission if applicable), numeric, nullable. NULL on all 139,760 rows (2026-10-07); no writer sets it. Unit: unknown (never written). Source: none. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.affiliate_link IS
'Intended referral link to the listing (creating migration: referral link for fair play), text, nullable. NULL on all 139,760 rows (2026-10-07); no writer sets it. Unit: none (URL). Source: none. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.sync_enabled IS
'Whether a live-sync job may refresh the row, boolean, nullable, default true. true on all 139,760 rows (2026-10-07); no writer ever set it false. Read by get_listings_needing_sync, check_auction_sync_health and check_sync_coverage, none of which a cron job or the repo calls. Unit: none (boolean). Source: column default. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.last_synced_at IS
'When a live-sync job last refreshed the row, timestamptz, nullable. Filled on 1,509 rows (1.1%, 2026-10-07): bat 1,496 (2025-12-31 .. 2026-01-21) and cars_and_bids 13 (2026-01-23); nothing has synced since 2026-01-23, so it is not a measure of freshness. Unit: timestamptz. Source: the former sync functions sync-bat-listing and sync-cars-and-bids-listing, both gone from the repo. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: writer time of the last sync.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.metadata IS
'Platform extras as written by the extractor, jsonb, nullable, default {}. NULL on 0 rows and {} on 6,193 (4.4%, 2026-10-07), mostly pcarmarket (307 of 310 pcarmarket rows in a 5% block sample are {}). Most of the 720 MB of TOAST of the table: bat rows average 6 KB with about 144 image URLs each. Keys (5% block sample, 6,791 rows): lot_number 6,428; source, comment_count, seller_username, buyer_username, image_count, reserve_status, images and image_urls about 5,100 each (every bat row; source extract-bat-core); extractor_version, auction_name and extraction_method 1,228 (barrettjackson, extractor 2.0.0, mostly embedded_json); chassis_number, estimate_low, estimate_high, estimate_currency, sale_id, sale_name, sale_location and quality_score 126 (bonhams); 30 smaller keys on fewer than 60 rows. metadata.reserve_status on bat rows: reserve_met, no_reserve, reserve_not_met. auto_mark_vehicle_sold_from_external_listing copies lot_number, seller_username, buyer_username and reserve_status to vehicles for sold bat rows. seller_username and buyer_username are public auction-site handles, returned to anon by get_vehicle_profile_data; none is quoted here. Unit: none (jsonb). Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: as of updated_at.';

-- ── Row clocks ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.created_at IS
'When the row was inserted: default now(), the transaction clock of the insert, never updated. Filled on every row (2026-10-07). Range 2025-12-07 .. 2026-04-14 02:36Z; by month: 2025-12 1,620, 2026-01 34,989, 2026-02 96,289, 2026-03 6,625, 2026-04 237; 138,887 distinct values. It is the time we first stored the listing, not when the listing appeared on the platform. Unit: timestamptz. Source: column default. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: ingest time of the first write.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.updated_at IS
'When a writer last stamped the row, timestamptz, nullable, default now(). No update trigger maintains it: the extractors sent their own clock (extract-bat-core sent new Date() with every insert and update) and sync_bid_count_to_external_listings sets now(); merge_vehicle_into_primary_by_url leaves it unchanged. Filled on every row (2026-10-07). By month: 2025-12 138, 2026-01 10,130, 2026-02 112,881, 2026-03 15,702, 2026-04 906, 2026-09 2, 2026-10 1; the 3 rows after 2026-04 were stamped by the bid-count trigger. Equal to created_at on 27,899 rows, later on 84,455 and earlier on 27,406 (19.6%: bat 25,126, pcarmarket 2,006; by a median of 0.07 s on bat and 0.10 s on pcarmarket, at most 63 s), consistent with the extractor stamping its own clock before the insert reached the database. Read as the recency key by vehicle_price_signal and enrich_cross_ref_ext_price. Unit: timestamptz. Source: the writer clock. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: writer time of the last write.';

DO $$
DECLARE
  missing text;
BEGIN
  SELECT string_agg(a.attname, ', ' ORDER BY a.attnum) INTO missing
  FROM pg_attribute a
  WHERE a.attrelid = 'public.external_listings'::regclass
    AND a.attnum > 0
    AND NOT a.attisdropped
    AND col_description(a.attrelid, a.attnum) IS NULL;
  IF missing IS NULL THEN
    RAISE NOTICE 'external_listings: every column has a comment';
  ELSE
    RAISE NOTICE 'external_listings columns still without a comment: %', missing;
  END IF;
END
$$;

COMMIT;
